      "description": "Takanock, LLC develops power-enabled sites and permanent on-site generation for data centers in power-constrained U.S. markets. The Traverse City-based platform combines land, entitlements, generation, fuel supply and grid interconnection to accelerate time to power for hyperscale and other large data-center customers, with disclosed activity including Northern Virginia and Phoenix. The operating business was formed in 2023, and the current Delaware LLC was formed in 2025. ArcLight and DigitalBridge became collective majority owners in an April 2025 equity financing and announced aggregate commitments of up to US$500 million on June 25, 2025; original investors retained a collective minority interest. Each sponsor's individual percentage, ArcLight fund and exact joint investment vehicle are not publicly disclosed.",
